From: Liang Zhen <gnailzenh@gmail.com>
Subject: [RFC PATCH] na: Add NA_Mem_handle_import_rkey() for third-party RDMA key import

Add a new NA-layer API that allows importing an externally-created RDMA
memory registration key (e.g., from NVIDIA cuFile/nvidia-fs) into a
Mercury NA memory handle, without performing local memory registration.

This enables storage systems like DAOS to receive a GPU buffer's RDMA
descriptor from cuFile's CUfileFSOps_t read/write callbacks (via the
cufileRDMAInfo_t parameter) and use it for direct GPU RDMA transfers
through Mercury's existing bulk transfer infrastructure.

The imported handle is treated as a remote handle — it can be used as
the remote_mem_handle in NA_Put()/NA_Get() operations, just like a
handle obtained from NA_Mem_handle_deserialize().

Implementation notes:
- UCX backend: Returns NA_OPNOTSUPPORTED. nvidia-fs produces raw verbs rkeys
  which are not ABI-compatible with UCX's ucp_rkey_pack() format. The caller
  (CaRT) falls back to normal bulk create with HMEM flags, which lets UCX
  handle CUDA memory natively via its own registration path.
- OFI backend: Constructs a remote handle from fi_mr_key + base address
  + length. The raw key is expected to be a uint64_t fi_mr_key (for
  providers using FI_MR_PROV_KEY) or the output of fi_mr_raw_attr().
- SM/BMI/MPI/PSM backends: Not supported (returns NA_OPNOTSUPPORTED).

Use case: NVIDIA GPUDirect Storage cuFile plugin
  When cuFile calls CUfileFSOps_t->read() with a non-NULL rdma_info,
  rdma_info->desc_str contains a serialized RDMA descriptor for the
  GPU buffer. The DAOS client can import this via:

    NA_Mem_handle_import_rkey(na_class, &remote_handle,
                             rdma_info->desc_str, rdma_info->desc_len,
                             remote_addr, size, NA_MEM_READWRITE);

  Then use remote_handle in bulk transfers — the server does RDMA
  directly to/from GPU memory without any Mercury-side GPU registration.

Signed-off-by: Liang Zhen <gnailzenh@gmail.com>
